cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Jev takes the bunker exam: a decision model on the dilemmas of The Philosophers"
message: "If you use this data, code or paper, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andreas
    family-names: Blum
    email: andreas.blum@tum.de
    city: Tacherting
    country: DE
repository-code: "https://github.com/Andymulb/jev_the_philosopher"
abstract: >-
  Experiment, data and paper for a study putting 39 moral dilemmas from the film
  The Philosophers (2013, also released as After the Dark) to Jev 1.13, a decision
  model that returns typed choices with probabilities instead of text. Every question
  was asked ten times through OpenRouter (410 requests). The model's answers were
  stable across runs but sensitive to how a dilemma was worded, and its decision time
  was independent of the difficulty of the question, in contrast to published human
  decision times.
keywords:
  - decision models
  - moral judgement
  - human-AI comparison
  - decision latency
  - AI ethics
  - trolley problem
